            <ArticleTitle>Multiplex Genome Editing in Escherichia coli.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>119-129</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/978-1-4939-7295-1_8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lambda Red recombineering is an easy and efficient method for generating genetic modifications in Escherichia coli. For gene deletions, lambda Red recombineering is combined with the use of selectable markers, which are removed through the action of, e.g., flippase (Flp) recombinase. This PCR-based engineering method has also been applied to a number of other bacteria. In this chapter, we describe a recently developed one plasmid-based method as well as the use of a strain with genomically integrated recombineering genes, which significantly speeds up the engineering of strains with multiple genomic alterations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
